{"id":157,"date":"2026-07-09T14:30:49","date_gmt":"2026-07-09T14:30:49","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/localhost:8181\/discreet-hvac-for-homes-inside-gettysburgs-historic-district\/"},"modified":"2026-07-15T21:04:09","modified_gmt":"2026-07-15T21:04:09","slug":"discreet-hvac-for-homes-inside-gettysburgs-historic-district","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/discreet-hvac-for-homes-inside-gettysburgs-historic-district\/","title":{"rendered":"Your Gettysburg Inn Guests Came for History, Not HVAC Noise"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover alignfull s-hero-cover\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:2rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:2rem\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-contrast-background-color has-background-dim-70 has-background-dim\"><\/span><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"697\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-198\" alt=\"brick rowhouse street\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/10787664563_3d35f30f8e_b.jpg\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/10787664563_3d35f30f8e_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/10787664563_3d35f30f8e_b-300x204.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/10787664563_3d35f30f8e_b-768x523.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-cover-is-layout-ff0c90b8 wp-block-cover-is-layout-constrained\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center has-base-color has-text-color s-hero-cover__title wp-block-heading\">Historic Comfort. Silent Systems.<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center s-lead has-base-color has-text-color has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">When your guests came for battlefield history, the last thing they should hear is your HVAC system rattling through the night.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-buttons-is-layout-35f06ea7 wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"\/contact\/\">Request a Quote<\/a><\/div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button is-style-outline is-style-outline--1\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link wp-element-button\" href=\"#content\">Learn More<\/a><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"s-trust-bar\"><div class=\"s-trust__item\">15+ Years Serving PA<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Licensed &amp; Insured<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Same-Day Emergency<\/div><div class=\"s-trust__item\">Local to Your Area<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Why Standard HVAC Fails These Homes<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Battlefield visitors expect period authenticity in their accommodations, but they also expect reliable heat in November and cool air in July. Gettysburg&#039;s bed-and-breakfast economy depends on historic properties\u2014Federal-style brick townhouses, Greek Revival farmhouses, Victorian mansions\u2014that were never designed for modern comfort systems. These homes have high ceilings, single-pane windows, and floor plans that resist conventional ductwork.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Installing forced air means cutting through plaster, compromising millwork, and routing ducts around chimneys and load-bearing walls. The noise alone can disrupt a guest experience. A furnace cycling in the basement or an air handler rumbling in the attic carries through old wood framing and reverberates in ways that modern drywall construction dampens. Window units block views and leak infiltration.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The solution isn&#039;t to avoid air conditioning or settle for less comfort\u2014it&#039;s to choose equipment and installation methods that respect the architecture while delivering the quiet, efficient climate control guests expect.<\/p>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-quote s-quote--accent has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote\"><blockquote><p>These homes need ductless solutions that respect the original architecture without tearing into hundred-and-fifty-year-old lathe.<\/p><cite>Gettysburg HVAC Specialist<\/cite><\/blockquote><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text\" style=\"grid-template-columns:50% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"minisplit - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1481\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-minisplit-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ductless Mini-Splits: Silent, Efficient, Invisible<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Ductless mini-split systems eliminate the need for bulky ductwork by delivering conditioned air directly to each room through slim wall-mounted or ceiling-recessed units. The outdoor condenser connects to indoor air handlers via refrigerant lines that run through small penetrations\u2014typically three-inch holes through exterior walls. This means no dropped ceilings, no soffit framing, and no compromised plaster or trim.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a Gettysburg B&amp;B with six guest rooms, each room can have its own air handler controlled independently, so unoccupied rooms don&#039;t waste energy. Modern inverter-driven mini-splits operate as low as 19 decibels\u2014quieter than a whisper. There&#039;s no central air handler cycling on and off, no ductwork amplifying fan noise, no rumble from a basement furnace traveling through floor joists.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For guests staying in a room above the kitchen, this silence matters. It&#039;s the difference between a restful night and a one-star review mentioning noise. Energy costs also favor ductless in seasonal operations. If the inn closes from January through March, individual room units can be shut down completely without affecting freeze protection.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A small amount of heat keeps pipes from bursting, but there&#039;s no need to condition guest spaces that won&#039;t be used. Over a winter season, that difference adds up to hundreds of dollars in wasted fuel.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-quote s-quote--mark has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote\"><blockquote><p>Ductless systems let you shut down individual rooms when unoccupied, keeping costs reasonable when half your property sits empty.<\/p><cite>Baltimore Street Inn Owner<\/cite><\/blockquote><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right\" style=\"grid-template-columns:auto 50%\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">High-Velocity Ducts for Tight Spaces<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When ceiling height is precious\u2014common in Greek Revival homes where first-floor rooms have ten-foot ceilings and second floors have eight\u2014high-velocity duct systems offer an alternative to conventional sheet metal. These systems use flexible two-inch ducts that snake through wall cavities and floor joists, terminating in small circular outlets that blend into walls or ceilings.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The air moves faster through smaller ducts, so the system delivers adequate volume without the bulk of traditional trunks and branches. Installation requires specialized equipment and trained contractors, but the result is air conditioning in a home that seemed impossible to retrofit without dropping ceilings or building soffits. High-velocity systems work especially well in balloon-framed homes where wall cavities run uninterrupted from basement to attic.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A single vertical chase can serve multiple rooms on different floors, with lateral runs kept short. The outlets produce a gentle whoosh rather than the rumble of a standard register, and many guests find it unobtrusive white noise rather than a disturbance. Proper location and vibration isolation minimize sound.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Placing the air handler in a conditioned attic or basement mechanical room, away from guest bedrooms, keeps noise out of living spaces. The result is cooling that never announces itself.<\/p>\n\n<\/div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/Ductless_Mini_Split_Heat_Pump_Installation.jpg\" alt=\"mini split heat pump\" class=\"wp-image-202\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/Ductless_Mini_Split_Heat_Pump_Installation.jpg 800w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/Ductless_Mini_Split_Heat_Pump_Installation-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/Ductless_Mini_Split_Heat_Pump_Installation-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 800px) 100vw, 800px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;Ductless Mini Split Heat Pump Installation&quot; by Vernon Air Con, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure><\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--cream has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-pills s-pills--glass\">\n<li>Ductless mini-splits operate at 19-23 dB \u2014 quieter than a guest room conversation<\/li>\n\n\n<li>High-velocity small-duct systems use 2-inch tubing that fits in existing wall cavities<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Historic properties: no exterior equipment visible from street per borough guidelines<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Seasonal-use properties need humidity control even when unoccupied to prevent plaster damage<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-quote s-quote--card has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote\"><blockquote><p>Historic preservation and energy efficiency aren&#039;t opposed goals. A well-conditioned room is more likely to preserve its plaster and finishes than a drafty, underheated one.<\/p><cite>Historic Property Consultant<\/cite><\/blockquote><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Solutions for Gettysburg&#039;s Summer Humidity<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gettysburg&#039;s summer climate combines heat with high humidity. Historic buildings absorb moisture, wood trim swells, and wallpaper loosens. Air conditioning helps, but undersized systems that cycle quickly cool the air without removing enough moisture. Proper dehumidification requires continuous operation or dedicated equipment.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list s-icon-list\">\n<li>Inverter-driven systems modulate capacity to maintain temperature while running continuously at lower speeds, maximizing moisture removal without short-cycling<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Dedicated dehumidifiers integrated with HVAC can target 50-55% relative humidity even when cooling demand is light, preventing musty smells<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Properly sized bath fans and range hoods exhaust moisture directly rather than circulating it through occupied rooms<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Portable dehumidifiers in basements and ground-floor rooms prevent mildew and protect finishes without oversizing the main system<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-overlap has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-10371125 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-overlap__img has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large alignwide\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/7823574634_1bc85772d4_b.jpg\" alt=\"cast iron radiator\" class=\"wp-image-181\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/7823574634_1bc85772d4_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/7823574634_1bc85772d4_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/7823574634_1bc85772d4_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;Cast Iron Radiator Refurbishment&quot; by gavindjharper, BY-ND, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-overlap__card has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-bfed0f9d wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:2.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:2.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Heating Without Destroying Historic Character<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Many Gettysburg inns already have functional heating\u2014baseboard hot water, cast-iron radiators, or original fireplaces supplemented by modern furnaces. The challenge is adding air conditioning without duplicating heating infrastructure. If radiators deliver reliable winter comfort, there&#039;s no reason to tear them out for forced air. Instead, a cooling-only ductless system or high-velocity setup provides summer relief while the hydronic system handles winter.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This dual approach preserves period heating elements that guests appreciate for their authenticity while delivering the modern comfort expectations that drive bookings. Heat pumps are increasingly viable for Gettysburg&#039;s climate, especially inverter-driven cold-climate models rated to work efficiently at temperatures below ten degrees Fahrenheit. A heat pump provides both heating and cooling without combustion, simplifying permitting in historic districts where adding fuel lines or venting exhaust requires preservation board approval.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Backup heat from electric resistance coils or a small gas furnace covers the coldest days, but those account for less than ten percent of annual heating hours.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--sand has-tint-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Complete HVAC Services for Historic Properties<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns alignwide s-feature-row is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-794e3cfa wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg\" alt=\"hvac technician repair\" class=\"wp-image-188\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;AC Service&quot; by SuperTech HVAC Services, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">System Design<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Custom cooling and heating plans that fit your building&#039;s architecture and preservation requirements.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1475\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-1.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ductless Installation<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Quiet mini-split systems with indoor units that blend seamlessly into period rooms.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"683\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1476\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-1024x683.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-300x200.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2-768x512.png 768w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez-technician-2.png 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gpt-image-1)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">High-Velocity Retrofit<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Small-duct systems for homes where conventional ductwork won&#039;t fit.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1755\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-1-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Maintenance &amp; Monitoring<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Seasonal pre-checks and smart controls for variable occupancy and energy savings.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"1024\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png\" alt=\"technician - professional HVAC service photo\" class=\"wp-image-1756\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2.png 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-300x300.png 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-150x150.png 150w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/ez2-technician-2-768x768.png 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--ai\" title=\"AI-generated (gemini-2.5-flash-image)\">AI<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Emergency Repairs<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Fast response for breakdowns during peak guest seasons.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column s-card s-feature-card is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-medium s-feature-card__img\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg\" alt=\"hvac technician repair\" class=\"wp-image-188\" srcset=\"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b.jpg 1024w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-300x225.jpg 300w, http:\/\/127.0.0.1:8181\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/07\/51282276312_f3389b56f2_b-768x576.jpg 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><span class=\"s-img-badge s-img-badge--stock\" title=\"&quot;AC Service&quot; by SuperTech HVAC Services, BY-SA, via Openverse\">Stock<\/span><\/figure>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Preservation Consultation<\/h3>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Guidance on borough approval, hidden equipment placement, and compatibility with historic standards.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--ink has-contrast-background-color has-background has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-diagnostic has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-b267b866 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:3rem;padding-right:3rem;padding-bottom:3rem;padding-left:3rem\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Guest Comfort Checkpoints for B&amp;B Owners<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>HVAC audible from guest rooms during quiet hours \u2014 equipment or ductwork noise transmission<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Temperature swings of 4+ degrees between floors \u2014 single-zone system in multi-story building<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Humidity complaints during summer stays \u2014 dehumidification inadequate for historic construction<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Window units visible from curb or dripping on siding \u2014 opportunity to upgrade aesthetics<\/li>\n\n\n<li>Seasonal startup delays \u2014 equipment dormant for months needs pre-season commissioning<\/li>\n\n<\/ul>\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group alignfull s-band s-band--warm-gradient has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-08713647 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:6rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:6rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;padding-left:2.5rem\">\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-element-heading has-text-align-center wp-block-heading\">Questions from Gettysburg Inn Operators<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group s-accordion s-accordion--minimal has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-1583283a wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\">\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Will installing ductless units affect my property&#039;s historic designation?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It depends on the specific designation and how the installation is executed. Interior changes that don&#039;t affect character-defining features generally don&#039;t require review. Exterior work\u2014like placing condensers or drilling penetrations on street-facing facades\u2014may need approval. Consulting with the historical review board early in the design process helps identify acceptable solutions before contractors begin work.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>How do I keep HVAC costs reasonable when half my rooms are empty most of the year?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Zone control is key. Ductless systems let you shut down individual rooms when unoccupied. Programmable thermostats or smart controls can reduce temperatures in unused spaces while maintaining comfort in occupied ones. For extended closures, setback temperatures keep pipes from freezing without conditioning the entire building to guest-ready levels.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>Can I add air conditioning without removing my radiators?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Absolutely. Radiators handle heating, and a separate cooling-only system\u2014ductless or high-velocity\u2014handles summer comfort. This avoids the cost and disruption of tearing out functional heating infrastructure. The two systems operate independently, so you&#039;re not paying for redundant heating capacity.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n\n<details class=\"wp-block-details is-layout-flow wp-block-details-is-layout-flow\"><summary>What&#039;s the noise level difference between mini-splits and traditional forced air?<\/summary>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Ductless mini-splits operate at 19-23 decibels\u2014comparable to a whisper. Conventional forced-air systems typically run at 40-50 decibels. That difference is noticeable in a quiet guest room, especially at night. High-velocity systems fall between the two, still quieter than traditional forced air but slightly louder than ductless.<\/p>\n\n<\/details>\n\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-633910b2 wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"padding-top:4.5rem;padding-right:2.5rem;padding-bottom:4.5rem;p